## Edge semantics

- `declares`: a task filing carries a typed route declaration.
- `gated by`: admission decides whether the declared route may proceed.
- `governs eligible pool`: DoE defines the population/policy constraints, not a preferred provider.
- `selects`: Scout binds task-fit to an eligible arm; exact runtime hand-off remains an open contract.
- `emits`: execution produces one canonical dispatch stamp.
- `fans out`: the same stamp is copied into multiple evidence planes; this is not multiple dispatches.
- `folded at publish`: the QUE collector incorporates watchdog claims into its producer-of-record queue feed.
- `projects`: Tribute Desk renders independent feed snapshots and does not execute dispatch.
- `composition unresolved`: the repository has not established a typed contract between task dispatch and invocation-level model routing.
